(D/'stage8_2_memory.md').write_text('# Native simulator resources\n\nArchitecture: Linux x86_64; no ARM runtime/resource qualification was attempted. The native image is not loadable on Cortex-M3.\n\n| Allocated section class | Bytes |\n|---|---:|\n| text | '+str(mem['text'])+' |\n| data | '+str(mem['data'])+' |\n| bss | '+str(mem['bss'])+' |\n\nHost memory at checkpoint: `'+json.dumps(mem['host_memory'])+'`. Configured reservations: `'+json.dumps(mem['reservations'])+'`. ELF/MAP/host BIN, section and symbol paths/hashes are in evidence/stage8_2/build/resources.json. The BIN is only a native artifact, not MCU firmware.\n\nOfficial UART framing buffer is 256 bytes; GDB DWARF size checks give each RX/TX ADU 262 bytes (252 data), context 712 bytes. RX and TX ADUs are separately stored in the context, sharing UART buffer across RX/TX. Their exact symbol sizes are in symbols.txt. Zephyr kernel heap reservation is 0; Host libc/malloc and native runner allocations are covered by Linux RSS, not a claimed MCU heap high-water.\n\n'+mem['stack_measurement_limit']+' The maximum observed Zephyr painted-stack used count is '+str(mem['max_observed_stack_used'])+' bytes; it is explicitly not the real host stack peak. Thread names/sizes and every observed watermark are retained. A zero-unused 40-byte POSIX placeholder is recorded rather than hidden or treated as a hardware stack overflow. No memory-fit or stack-safety claim for Cortex-M3 is made.\n')
items=['Zephyr Modbus Compatibility','Modbus RTU Slave','Independent Host Master','PTY Bidirectional Communication','Function Codes','CRC16','GPIO Output Mapping','GPIO Input Mapping','Register Map','Exception Handling','Fault Injection','1000 Transactions','Resource Analysis','Stage 0–8.1 Regression']
(D/'stage8_2_report.md').write_text('# Stage 8.2 acceptance\n\nStage 8.2 SOFTWARE PASS.\n\n| Item | Result |\n|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join('| '+i+' | PASS |' for i in items)+'\n| Physical RS485 | NOT TESTED |\n| Hardware | NOT TESTED |\n\nIndependent pymodbus 3.11.4 / pyserial 3.5 exchanges actual PTY bytes with unmodified Zephyr v4.4.2 RTU framing/CRC and standard handlers. A documented application preflight shim prevents partial configuration writes and supplies correct application-value exceptions. Current native PTY cannot apply runtime serial settings; requested 115200 8E1 is software configuration and Host parity is disabled after EINVAL. This is not a physical UART/RS485 test.\n\nNormal successful transactions: '+str(t['successful_transactions'])+' including a dedicated 1000-transaction consistency loop. New executed groups: '+str(t['tests']+1)+'; history: '+str(reg['stage0_7'])+'/133 plus Stage8.1 '+str(reg['stage8_1_new'])+' groups, all passed. Owned-process termination cleanup also passed. Faults cover CRC, unit ID, function/address/value/quantity, incomplete and fragmented frames, reconnect, cross-boundary and invalid-later-value atomic rejection. Absolute writes have no hidden retries (master retries=0); RTU has no transaction-ID exactly-once guarantee.\n\nRequest categories are separately recorded in evidence/stage8_2/fault/statistics.json; valid means CRC-valid addressed requests including exception-producing requests. Final device counters: `'+json.dumps(t['stats'])+'`. Final register/GPIO state: `'+json.dumps(t['final'])+'`. RX counts include invalid frames; response counter means prepared responses. Independent wire logs establish Host delivery. CRC/incomplete/wrong-unit drops are not included in successful transaction counts. DE/RE returns to RX at checkpoint and actual GPIO transitions are recorded.\n\nFailed initial build/wire attempts are retained: missing ensurepip (resolved with isolated no-pip venv plus pip --python), PTY parity EINVAL, and whole-port masked GPIO read semantics. The first stack check exposed a native 40-byte placeholder; resource report records the real measurement limitation instead of claiming MCU stack watermarks.\n\nReproduce: python3 scripts/stage8_2_setup_master.py, then python3 scripts/accept_stage8_2.py --mode all. All mode performs fresh Stage8.1 and Stage0–7 regression in isolated evidence directories. All logs, ELF and wire traces remain under ../modbus_stage8_2_ws. Earlier source/evidence is protected; only an optional historical evidence-output helper changes. No root, system Python, ROS environment or Zephyr version changes.\n\nBaseline: 37363f3. Delivery revision is recorded in Git. Stage8.3, TCP, CAN, RS485 electrical tests and hardware operations were not performed.\n')
protected=subprocess.check_output(['git','ls-tree','-r','--name-only','37363f3','evidence'],cwd=R,text=True).splitlines();subprocess.run(['git','diff','--exit-code','37363f3','--',*protected],cwd=R,check=True)
